	<!-- ─── Troubleshooting ────────────────────────────────── -->
	<section id="troubleshooting" class="scroll-mt-16">
		<div class="mx-auto max-w-[1200px] px-4 py-20 sm:px-6 md:py-24">
			<div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl">
				<p class="eyebrow">troubleshooting</p>
				<h2 class="mt-3 text-display-lg text-ink">When your compass points the wrong way.</h2>
				<p class="mt-3 text-body-lg text-body">
					A misbehaving compass is almost always an interference problem, not a broken sensor.
					Work through these checks in order.
				</p>
				<div class="mt-8 space-y-4">
					<div class="card-soft p-5">
						<h3 class="text-sm font-medium text-ink mb-1">The dial spins or the number climbs nonstop</h3>
						<p class="text-sm leading-6">You are near a strong magnetic source. Remove MagSafe cases and magnetic mounts, move away from speakers, motors, and metal, then recalibrate.</p>
					</div>
					<div class="card-soft p-5">
						<h3 class="text-sm font-medium text-ink mb-1">The reading is steady but seems a few degrees off</h3>
						<p class="text-sm leading-6">That is usually declination. Toggle on true north and enable location so the correction applies to your exact coordinates.</p>
					</div>
					<div class="card-soft p-5">
						<h3 class="text-sm font-medium text-ink mb-1">Nothing happens when I tap the button</h3>
						<p class="text-sm leading-6">Sensor access requires a secure HTTPS page and a device with a magnetometer. Check that you granted motion and orientation permission for this site.</p>
					</div>
					<div class="card-soft p-5">
						<h3 class="text-sm font-medium text-ink mb-1">It works on my phone but not my laptop</h3>
						<p class="text-sm leading-6">Most laptops have no magnetometer, so there is nothing to read. Use your phone for live headings; the computer still shows the demo dial and sun and moon data.</p>
					</div>
					<div class="card-soft p-5">
						<h3 class="text-sm font-medium text-ink mb-1">The needle lags when I turn quickly</h3>
						<p class="text-sm leading-6">Smoothing keeps the reading stable, so it trails fast spins slightly. Slow down for a moment and the number will settle.</p>
					</div>
				</div>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

